            text: "Almost always because more stain was applied than the wood could absorb. Penetrating stain cures by soaking into the fibre; whatever cannot get in sits on the surface as a film that oil-based products in particular cannot harden. Cold weather, high humidity, damp wood, mill glaze and a previous finish all reduce absorption and make the same over-application worse.",
