        </ul>

        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            A sticky deck is stain that could not get into the wood. Give it 72 hours in decent weather; if it is still tacky, wipe the excess off with mineral-spirits-dampened rags, or re-wet it with a thin coat of fresh stain and wipe that off. That fixes the vast majority of cases in an afternoon.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Only if it will not cure after that do you strip and start again. Next time, test the wood with water, wait for it to dry, watch the forecast, apply what it will take, and back-brush everything. And lay the rags out flat before you go to bed.
          </p>
        </div>

